TITLE: [ROM][17][OFFICIAL][cheetah] ExpressiveOS 1.0 — First Bloom

[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]ExpressiveOS 1.0 — First Bloom, now on six Pixels[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]First public release · Android 17 · six Pixels on day one[/I][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

Today ExpressiveOS goes public for the first time.

ExpressiveOS is built around one simple idea: add to the Pixel experience, and never take anything away. That means unlimited room to make the phone yours, with a launcher, theming and holiday looks built in. It also means keeping what your Pixel already does, right down to the stock firmware, modem and IMS.

ExpressiveOS 1.0, "First Bloom", is out now on Android 17, on six phones at once, from the Pixel 7 Pro to the Pixel 11 Pro Fold. You can install it right from your browser.

A first bloom is the first flower a plant opens, and this one is ours. It's also a thank-you: reports from our Telegram group shaped this release, and without Loïc, this ROM would never have happened.

[CENTER]{{SCREENSHOTS}}[/CENTER]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]✨ What's in ExpressiveOS 1.0[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]1. 🏠 Expressive Launcher, built in[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Expressive Launcher 5.0.9 is your Home screen, and it also runs Recents, so Overview, swipe up and quick switch all go through it. It's derived from Lawnchair and AOSP Launcher3.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=4][B]2. 🎨 Studio, with the Bloom look[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Studio (Expressive Studio), in Settings, puts ExpressiveOS's customization in one place. It opens on a bento-style set of tiles: a live lock screen preview, Themes, Wallpaper & style, Colors (your Monet palette), Fonts and Lock screen clocks, plus tiles for Status bar, Quick settings, Notifications, Power menu and Miscellaneous.
[*]The Bloom petal logo and its violet, blue, coral and green palette run through Settings. The Bloom wallpaper greets you on first boot.
[*]What's new, at the bottom of Studio, shows the release notes.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=4][B]3. 🎃 Holiday themes[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]In Studio > Holiday themes, ExpressiveOS can dress your phone up for 8 holidays a year: wallpaper, colours, Settings icons, a holiday picture in the Quick Settings header, the lock screen clock and boot animation colours, and a greeting card at the top of Settings.
[*]On Automatic, a theme switches on by itself at the first screen-off after midnight on the holiday's first day, and off again after its last day. Then everything is put back.
[*]A quiet notification lets you skip it for the year, and you can try any theme early from the same page.
[*]Next up is Thanksgiving. Its theme starts Monday, November 23.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=4][B]4. 🔄 Updates over the air[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]The built-in Updater checks for new ExpressiveOS releases and installs them over the air. No computer needed.
[*]From the next release, it also offers a smaller update made for the exact build you're on, next to the full one.
[*]Downloaded an update package yourself? Open the Updater's menu and tap Install local update.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=4][B]5. 🔓 Root is your choice[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]ExpressiveOS ships without root, and nothing in it needs root. If you want root, adding it is up to you.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=4][B]6. 📶 Your carrier features stay[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]The stock Pixel firmware, modem and IMS are kept, so calls, VoLTE and Wi-Fi Calling run on the same parts as on stock Android.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=4][B]7. 🎬 Its own boot animation[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Drawn for ExpressiveOS from the Bloom logo and wordmark. Its motion was inspired by a concept by Loïc, a member of our community.

[/LIST]
[SIZE=4][B]8. 🎧 Audio effects on the Pixel 7 Pro[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Pixel 7 Pro only: ViPER4Android RE audio effects are built in, with the ViPER4Android RE app and the ViPERFX_RE effect library. App: [URL="https://github.com/likelikeslike/ViPER4Android"]https://github.com/likelikeslike/ViPER4Android[/URL]

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

