[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]💻 Install it from your browser[/B][/SIZE]

The new web installer lists all six phones and walks you through 6 steps: Phone, Build, Download, Connect, Install, Done. Open it at [URL="https://expressiveos-flash.daryldenson-apps.workers.dev"]https://expressiveos-flash.daryldenson-apps.workers.dev[/URL].

[LIST]
[*][B]You'll need[/B]: a USB cable that carries data, about 30 minutes, and Chrome or Edge on a computer (or Chrome on an Android phone connected to the Pixel with a cable).
[*][B]Before you start[/B]: back up. Coming from stock Android or another ROM, installing wipes the phone, and unlocking the bootloader also erases everything. Update the phone to the latest stock Android 17 first.
[*][B]It does the fiddly parts[/B]: with USB debugging on, it finds your phone while it's running Android and restarts it into Fastboot Mode for you. It can also unlock the bootloader after you confirm. OEM unlocking must be on in Developer options, and some carrier phones can't be unlocked.
[*][B]After installing[/B]: keep the bootloader unlocked. Locking it with ExpressiveOS installed stops the phone from starting. The first start takes a few minutes. From then on, updates arrive through the built-in Updater.
[*][B]Stuck on the boot animation for more than 15 minutes?[/B] Hold Power and Volume down to get back to Fastboot Mode, then install again with a clean install.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]💐 Thank you[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Loïc, first and always.[/B] Without him, this ROM would never have happened. His concept inspired how the boot animation moves, and he offered to translate ExpressiveOS into French. The About page has a Special thanks card for him.
[*][B]Our Telegram group.[/B] Your reports shaped this release. Thank you for every one of them.
[*][B]The open source work underneath.[/B] LineageOS and AOSP, our base. Evolution X's open source code, our starting point. Lawnchair, where the launcher's roots are. The ViPER4Android RE developers, for the Pixel 7 Pro audio effects. And Google Sans Flex, the OFL font in our branding.

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]😄 Launch Humor[/B][/SIZE]

[QUOTE]🌸 [I]Six Pixels agreed that nobody blooms first, so they all walked in together. The Fold still made the biggest entrance, mostly by opening.[/I][/QUOTE]

[QUOTE]🔌 [I]The web installer asks for a USB cable that carries data. Somewhere, a drawer full of charge-only cables is feeling very seen.[/I][/QUOTE]

[QUOTE]🏠 [I]The app drawer doesn't blur Home yet, so your Home screen can watch you hunt for apps. It isn't judging. It's just proud of you.[/I][/QUOTE]

[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]💬 Community Notes[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Who it's for[/B]: owners of the six phones above, with one build for each phone.
[*][B]Still being worked on[/B]:
[LIST]
[*]The Updater doesn't show the release notes yet, but What's new in Studio does. Fixed in the next release.
[*]Expressive Launcher's app drawer doesn't blur the Home screen behind it yet, so you can see Home through the drawer. A fix is ready for the next release.
[/LIST]
[*][B]Validation[/B]:
[LIST]
[*][B]Pixel 7 Pro[/B]: this exact build was installed over the air through the Updater on a Pixel 7 Pro and rebooted three times. The launcher, the audio effects, the Wi-Fi Calling app and a holiday theme were checked, and the phone's logs showed no crashes or freezes. A later re-check of the same phone was clean too.
[*][B]Pixel 8 Pro[/B]: built from the same sources as the Pixel 7 Pro build, which was checked on a phone with no crashes or freezes.
[*][B]Pixel 11 phones[/B]: built from the same ExpressiveOS sources, on Google's own Pixel 11 kernel and vendor images. Every build passes the build system's automatic checks before it's packed.
[/LIST]
[*][B]Help and feedback[/B]: questions, bug reports and first impressions are welcome in [URL="https://t.me/ExpressiveGroup"]@ExpressiveGroup[/URL].

[/LIST]
[HR][/HR]

[SIZE=5][B]🧩 Release Riddle[/B][/SIZE]

[QUOTE][I]I'm a lunch box you can't eat from. One compartment holds your colours, one your fonts, one your clocks, and one shows your lock screen live. What am I?[/I][/QUOTE]

[SPOILER="Tap to reveal answer"][B]Studio![/B] Its home screen is a bento-style set of tiles, from Colors and Fonts to Lock screen clocks, plus a live lock screen preview. It's in Settings. 🍱[/SPOILER]

[HR][/HR]

